     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Consultations with the HRDO held.
3. Discussions with the staff of the HRDO are held, trainings needs identified.
8. Training needs identified.
12. Operation of the e-rights platform monitored.
16. Training for the patrol officers in Yerevan completed and in marzes launched.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1 Consultations held, needs assessment of training needs conducted. 
3. Training needs on UN HR Treaty Bodies identified ( to be implemented jointly with OHCHR in 2022)
8. Training needs of the Office of the Representative of Legal Matters identified to be conducted in 2022
12. E-rights platform monitored, follow up actions discuss with the MoJ
16. Trainings in Yerevan conducted and completed, trainings in Shirak and Lori regions launched in November.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Needs assessment provided, capacity building organised.
2. 2 trainings organised.
3. At least two trainings are organised.
6. Consultations conducted, needs assessed.
7. ToRs developed.
8. At least two trainings organised.
9. Public awareness campaign launched.
10. 2 trainings conducted.
11. One module introduced.
12. Evaluation of the Plan kicked off.
13. Consultations on the drafting process.
14. 1 public awareness product prepared.
15. Police officers of Shirak and Lori regions trained.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Preliminary needs assessment organised to be followed by capacity building exercised; 
2. A series of trainings and discussions organised for the NPM to monitor the conditions of individuals in closed institutions; knowledge product developed;
3. 2 Trainings on the new Criminal Procedure Code organised, checklist on the provisions of the new legislation prepared
6. Consultations in place, technical assistance provided, the office to be established in January 2023. 
7 Needs assessed, certain aspects being covered by other international organisations.
8. 3 trainings, discussions organised relating to the functions of the office and cooperation with other state agencies.
9. Human Rights Contest and public awareness campaign on the engagement of female in the police and law-enforcement launched.
10. 5 trainings provided to the project beneficiaries on various aspects of human rights protection.
11. A separate training module organised for the trainers of the new patrol police service trainings.
12. The evaluation of the current work plan has kicked off, and the development of the new Plan is underway.
13. Consultations on the new draft has been kicked off, two sectoral discussions took place.
14. 2 Posters and 4 banners developed.
15. 5-months trainings for police officers of Shirak and Lori regions completed.</narrative>
      </comment>
